\f1\fs22 Chainsaw met Sarah at the front door and wound herself around her calves, then followed Sarah down the hall to the family room. The lights were on outside; Sarah found Kathy and Hayley sitting at the table on the patio. Hayley had a glass of white wine; Kathy had no need for alcohol.\
\'93Ah, you brought it,\'94 Hayley said, recognising the antique holoscreen under Sarah\'92s arm; Hayley had only ever seen it sleeping on a credenza in Sarah\'92s office.\
Sarah slid onto the bench next to Hayley, and powered up the antique box. Within a few seconds it cast a three-dimensional array of wispy pictorial interfaces above it at comfortable viewing height.\
\'93She stole it from a museum,\'94 Kathy explained to Hayley.\
\'93I did not,\'94 Sarah said.\
\'93She got it out of a dumpster out back of a museum,\'94 Kathy replied.\
\'93Don\'92t you be dissing my holoscreen. It was my mother\'92s.\'94\
\'93Did 
\f2\i she
\f1\i0  get it from a museum?\'94\
\'93It\'92s a family heirloom.\'94\
\'93Going back\'97what?\'97twenty generations?\'94\
Sarah laughed. \'93You sound like Chanta. He called it 
\f2\i beta
\f1\i0 \'97or something like that\'97the first time he saw it.\'94\
\'93So nothing can monitor it here?\'94 Hayley asked.\
\'93Modern networks are sniffing several layers above where this operates. They don\'92t even know it\'92s here.\'94\
Hayley produced a thumb drive from a pocket; Sarah connected it to her adapter. The holoscreen considered the device for a couple of seconds and made a noise like a full service of cutlery being dropped in another room. A new directory appeared in the array of interfaces hovering above the table.\
\'93It\'92s sharper than I would have thought,\'94 Hayley conceded and stroked the stem of her wine glass then pointed to a line on the fresh directory.\
Sarah gestured to shut the other display, then opened the document. Hayley pointed at two more lines and Sarah opened those.\
Hayley gave them a short version of Lysander Preservation Research, its circuitous route back to Shakti Enterprises, and why Fridge Force had shut it down. She summarised closed resonance and the apparent capability of directing and shaping field responses of the kind that showed up in the Goa-Rotherhithe event.\
\'93So Eloise was doing weapons development,\'94 Kathy concluded.\
\'93Fridge Force could have made that accusation, but didn\'92t,\'94 Hayley said.\
\'93Even so,\'94 Kathy said and shrugged.\
\'93
\f2\i The demonstrated effects have plausible military application
\f1\i0 ,\'94 Sarah read and quoted.\
\'93Do you suppose Johnny has access to any of this material?\'94 Hayley asked Sarah.\
\'93I doubt he needs it. The Sages seem to have just the answer to feed him.\'94\
\'93I\'92m surprised they\'92re still here,\'94 Kathy said.\
\'93I\'92ve killed their access credentials,\'94 Hayley said. \'93Several times. Somehow they just keep showing up.\'94\
\'93They do that,\'94 Sarah observed. \'93I doubt they\'92d have any less influence if I shot them to the moon.\'94\
\'93I suppose they help Johnny look good,\'94 Kathy reflected. \'93And Eloise knows where progress is coming from.\'94\
Sarah skimmed through the files. After a while she said, \'93Nowhere does this material say this was stasis research.\'94\
\'93I noticed that too,\'94 Hayley said. \
Sarah moved through several pages. \'93They were trying to stop fields interfering.\'94\
\'93At first.\'94\
\'93And then they started making them interfere.\'94\
\'93Deliberately.\'94\
Sarah enlarged one of the diagrams.\
Hayley pointed. \'93They could concentrate and relocate resonance responses. Tens of metres in those tests.\'94\
\'93And Fridge Force stopped it.\'94\
Sarah returned to the technical assessment and moved backwards through the figures. \'93Show me the phase material again.\'94\
Hayley found it. Sarah read it twice, then opened a file from the holoscreen\'92s solid state.\
\'93What\'92s that?\'94 Hayley asked.\
\'93Project Kebab data,\'94 Sarah said and put one of the recent pattern sets beside the old research.\
Hayley moved closer. \
\'93What are you looking for?\'94 Kathy asked.\
\'93Not sure,\'94 Sarah said.\
\'93That\'92s reassuring.\'94\
Sarah moved through several received patterns, stopping at the cleaner ones.\
\'93When Johnny talks about improving the signal, he\'92s talking about coherence.\'94\
\'93Okay.\'94 Hayley waited for more.\
Sarah traced a repeating structure with one finger. \'93He\'92s been treating these as messages.\'94\
\'93Which means that\'92s how the Sages are treating them.\'94\
\'93Or that\'92s their cover story.\'94\
Hayley looked at Sarah.\
Sarah enlarged another section. \'93Look. There are relationships inside them. Repeated states. Relative positions. Timing. Maybe phase.\'94\
The other two stayed quiet and let her think. \'93We don\'92t know where the message stops and the field behaviour begins,\'94 Sarah said.\
Sarah\'92s holoscreen had no physical keyboard, but she seemed to be making precise gestures in the air with her fingers like she was engaging in fine control of the machine.\
A three-dimensional  image appeared above the holoscreen and slowly rotated.\
Sarah explained, \'93This shows the energy scars of the lab after Johnny blew it up the first time. The first time I saw them, I recognised the patterns from the nightmares I was having.\'94 After a few more gestures Sarah had thrown more images in the air above the table.\
\'93Similar pattern,\'94 Kathy said.\
\'93Yes,\'94 Sarah confirmed. \'93They\'92re projections from test data of successive Project Kebab spins.\'94\
\'93Have you still been dreaming them?\'94 Hayley asked.\
\'93She hasn\'92t,\'94 Kathy answered for Sarah. \'93Once Sarah realised what she was looking at, the nightmares stopped.\'94\
Sarah\'92s gestures sped up and became more emphatic. \'93I\'92m preparing an analysis of the technical data on the public record.\'94 After well over a minute of that, Sarah sat back and exhaled. \'93This might take a while.\'94 She watched Hayley sip her wine and envied her.\
The Three Sisters sat in silence until new images populated the air alongside Project Kebab material. Sarah cleared everything away except the images from new data. Sarah could feel them all thinking the same thing.\
\'93You can see which images come from one kebab\'85\'94 Kathy pointed as she spoke. \'93\'85 two kebabs, three kebabs.\'94\
\'93Yep,\'94 Hayley agreed.\
Sarah nodded. After a few moments she removed the thumb drive and shut down the holoscreen.\
Hayley reached for it. \'93
\f2\i Medical applications in times of armed conflict
\f1\i0 ,\'94 she quoted. \'93Medical applications were the cover story back then. Interdimensional communication is Project Kebab\'92s.\'94\
\'93Two projects funded by the same person,\'94 Kathy said, while Sarah looked into her hands resting on her swollen belly. \'93Who profits from the threat of armed conflict.\'94
